

⭐ THE REALITY OF GITHUB INTEGRATION (CMB‑style, stripped down)

1. Your viewer needs to do only ONE THING with GitHub:

Take a GitHub link → turn it into a usable file → load it.

That’s it.

Everything else is optional convenience.

2. There are only TWO ways a viewer can access GitHub files:

A. Public URL → Raw file

GitHub’s “blob” links are NOT real files.You convert them to “raw” links, and now they’re real files.

Example:

blob → raw

Viewer loads it. Done.

B. Local clone

If the repo is on your machine, the viewer just reads the files directly.

No magic. No API. No tokens.

3. File pairing is simple:

If you load:

run_001.mp4

The viewer looks for:

run_001.data.json
run_001.cmb

If they exist → attach them.If not → just play the video.

This is automatic wiring, not a complicated system.

4. UI needs only TWO buttons:

Open from GitHub URL

Open Local Repo

That’s it.

Everything else is optional sugar.

5. Version awareness is optional

If the viewer sees a .git folder, it can read:

branch

commit

tag

If not, it just loads the file normally.















